= Working memory — Technical =

== Multicomponent framework ==
The Baddeley model distinguishes specialized temporary systems coordinated by executive control.

Later versions add an episodic buffer to integrate information across domains and long-term memory.

The central executive is a functional construct, not a literal inner agent.

== Embedded-processes model ==
Cowan's framework treats working memory as activated long-term memory plus a capacity-limited focus of attention.

This shifts emphasis from separate storage buffers toward activation and attentional state.

== Capacity models ==
Models include discrete-slot, flexible-resource, interference, temporal-context, and continuous-resource accounts.

Observed item limits depend on task structure, feature complexity, precision, chunking, and prior knowledge.

== Neural implementation ==
Persistent neural firing is one proposed maintenance mechanism, but activity-silent synaptic states and dynamic population codes can also support temporary retention.

No one neural signature defines all working memory.

== References ==
* Baddeley (2012), ''Annual Review of Psychology'' 63:1–29.
